-- DEMO-DATA-PR-003. One-time correction of the 69 replayed Cheongdam visits: the replay had stored a
-- category word ("진료", "재진", ...) as visit_purpose. This writes the reception sentence from
-- scripts/demo-data/cheongdam-chart-history.data.mjs into visit_purpose and chief_complaint, the two
-- columns the reception form fills with the same text. Rows are matched by patient and check-in time.
-- session_replication_role = replica keeps updated_at on the visit day (the only trigger on
-- public.encounters is set_encounters_updated_at). The block fails, and so rolls back, unless exactly
-- 69 rows change. A fresh replay needs no correction: the engine now passes this text at reception.
do $fix$
declare n int;
